Third-party work the built images contain or download
-----------------------------------------------------

jellyfin-ffmpeg 8.1.3-1 (the worker image). GNU General Public License,
version 3 or later. Installed from the package the Jellyfin project
publishes; its copyright file is in the image at
/usr/share/doc/jellyfin-ffmpeg8/copyright. Source:
https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-ffmpeg at tag v8.1.3-1. Hikari Index
runs ffmpeg and ffprobe as separate programs and does not modify them.

IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Mono (the gallery). SIL Open Font License 1.1;
see gallery/static/fonts/LICENSE-IBM-Plex.txt.

Model weights (the inference base, the analyze workers and the text
encoder download these at build time from Hugging Face, at pinned
revisions, and the built images contain them). Licences as stated on
each model page at the pinned revision, checked 2026-10-03:

  SigLIP 2, google/siglip2-base-patch16-224            Apache License 2.0
  WD SwinV2 tagger v3, SmilingWolf/wd-swinv2-tagger-v3 Apache License 2.0
  hysts/anime-face-detector-faster-rcnn                MIT License
  hysts/anime-face-detector-hrnetv2                    MIT License
  deepghs/anime_head_detection (head_detect_v2.0_s)    MIT License
  deepghs/anime_person_detection (person_detect_v1.3_s) MIT License
  aslakey/camera_angle (fine-tune of                   Apache License 2.0
    facebook/dinov2-with-registers-large, Apache-2.0)

The two deepghs detectors (checked 2026-10-06) were trained with
Ultralytics YOLOv8, and their files name Ultralytics' AGPL-3.0 licence
in their metadata; Hikari Index is AGPL-3.0 as well. The
anime-face-detector Python package is MIT, and onnxruntime, which runs
the deepghs detectors, is MIT. aslakey/camera_angle (checked 2026-10-06)
states Apache-2.0 on its model card. A model page can
change; read it again before you redistribute an image.

NVIDIA CUDA and cuDNN runtime libraries (the GPU analyze image only; the
CPU analyze image and the text encoder contain none). They arrive as the
nvidia-* packages PyTorch depends on and are not modified. They are
proprietary: the CUDA libraries under NVIDIA's End User License
Agreement and cuDNN under NVIDIA's licence agreement for software
development kits. Both allow the runtime libraries to be distributed as
part of an application that does more than they do, unmodified, for use
on systems with NVIDIA GPUs, under terms consistent with NVIDIA's, and
both say the libraries must not be made subject to an open source
licence. Hikari Index's licence covers Hikari Index's own code; it does
not extend to these libraries, which stay under NVIDIA's terms. NCCL is
BSD-licensed. The full texts are in the image, in each package's
License.txt under
/opt/conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/nvidia_*.dist-info/. No NVIDIA
driver library is in the image; those come from the host.

PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause) and the third-party code it bundles: its LICENSE
and NOTICE are in the image under
/opt/conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/torch-*.dist-info/.

Everything else the images install comes from PyPI, npm, crates.io and
Debian under its own licence, recorded in each package's metadata.
